1- Feature Encoding: Boolean questionnaire responses are mapped to binary integers (True→1, False→0).
2- Feature Selection: SelectKBest with the ANOVA F-test ranks all 30 NMS features by their discriminative power. The optimal k=17 features are retained, determined by grid search over k ∈ {10,15,17,20,25,30} maximizing 5-fold CV balanced accuracy on the training set. 3- Stratified Split: The dataset is partitioned into training (80%) and test (20%) sets with stratification to preserve class proportions across splits. 4- SMOTE Balancing: The Synthetic Minority Oversampling Technique [20] is applied exclusively to the training partition, generating synthetic minority-class samples. Crucially, the test set remains untouched to ensure unbiased evaluation. 5- Model Training & CV: 5-fold stratified cross-validation with grid-search hyperparameter tuning is performed on the balanced training set. Final models are retrained on the full balanced training set using optimal hyperparameters. 6- Evaluation: Models are evaluated on the held-out test set using balanced accuracy (primary metric), precision, recall, and F1-score. Separate evaluations are performed for PD vs. HC and PD vs. DD.
